extbackslash displaystyle W\^\{(n)\}\}    converges in distribution to a standard Brownian motion                         W         :=         (         W         (         t         )                    )                        t             {$\in$}             [             0             ,             1             ]                                     \{\textbackslash displaystyle W:=(W(t))\_\{t\textbackslash in [0,1]\}\}    as                         n         \textrightarrow{}         {$\infty$}         .                 \{\textbackslash displaystyle n\textbackslash to \textbackslash infty .\}},
